# Everything here is regenerable: the data set is a public download, the venv is
# built from requirements.txt, and out*/ plus features*.npz are script output.
# Together they are about 1.8 GB, which is not something to carry in git.
tinyml/data/
tinyml/.venv/
tinyml/out*/
tinyml/features*.npz

# NOT ignored, and deliberately: tinyml/captures-door-*.csv holds the labelled
# walk-ups modules/woz_ml/ is trained on. Those are not a public download and
# their only other copy is capture logs on one laptop, so the set the shipped
# thresholds come from lives in the tree. CSV rather than .npz because the
# mal-diff gate blocks binary blobs, and it is right to: 17 KB of text is
# reviewable, a pickle-capable archive is not.
